{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1528884-how-do-hunter-compact-and-conspiracy-deal-with-supernatural-mortal","id":1528884,"title":"How do Hunter Compact and Conspiracy Deal with Supernatural Mortal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-19T03:03:14-08:00","id":1528884,"title":"How do Hunter Compact and Conspiracy Deal with Supernatural Mortal?","content":"Like some Mortal have Supernatural Ability that aren't from being a Hunter, but they also aren't any of the Major Splat, how do the different Compact and Conspiracy Deal with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 01-19-2024, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T07:01:59-08:00","id":1528915,"title":"","content":"It's going to vary, a lot. A psychic vampire who walks around killing people is probably going to get targeted by hunters before a vampire who is living peacefully and eating animals, but a regular human who just happens to have a bit of telepathy or telekinesis isn't going to be a target for most hunter groups. Unless of course they think perhaps they can put his brain in a jar and make drugs to grant themselves telepathy or TK...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T07:08:22-08:00","id":1528920,"title":"","content":"I wonder how would the Hunter Deal with The Plain, who remind me of the Matyr from Hunter the Reckoning, they even got their own Hunter Net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T07:02:28-08:00","id":1529005,"title":"","content":"RAW, if a hunter knows that the mortal's capabilities are not &quot;Dread Powers&quot; but Supernatural Merits, they should be treated as &quot;people&quot; by the Code.<br /> <br /> My personal take- this is impossible to actually be verified in an OOC manner. If the hunter comes from a org which has an ideology that accepts that mortals should have access to supernatural abilities (at least a certain &quot;type&quot; of them or under certain restrains/criteria), they are treated as &quot;people&quot; Otherwise, it is likely that they will be treated as &quot;monsters&quot;. For example, a Council of Bones hunter views any capacity to use supernatural power as tainted unless granted by Death- they don't necessary want to kill the character, but they might see them as either &quot;corrupted&quot; if they don't serve Death or as &quot;potential recruit&quot; if they think that Death has blessed them with their merits- it is likely that most people with such Merits would be treated as the later unless their powers could not be tied to Death whatsoever or if they use them to cause violent acts which produce ghosts/abuse them. TFV are likely to just accept that there are people with strange powers and be done with it, potentially monitoring them or trying to recruit them. KoSG are unlikely to be able to efficiently differentiate them from witches, and as such to the stake they go. Lucifuge hunters might view them as touched by demons and will keep one eye open on them, but will not target them specifically. Le Mysteres will see them as blessed individuals, gifted by the spirits. Cheiron would really want to conduct research upon them, but probably will not just butcher them- instead more likely to just try and pay them enough so they would &quot;volunteer&quot; to their experiments. <br /> <br /> In short, highly dependent on org and actual knowledge that a certain group has on the supernatural- the more they know, the easier it is for them to differentiate a mortal with supernatural quirks from a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T17:51:56-08:00","id":1529056,"title":"","content":"How does the Hunter recongize Mortal With Supernatural Merit and Minor Template (or whatever it's call now), from human Splat like The Bound, or Deviant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T19:55:28-08:00","id":1529061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1528884-how-do-hunter-compact-and-conspiracy-deal-with-supernatural-mortal?p=1529056#post1529056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Hunter recongize Mortal With Supernatural Merit and Minor Template (or whatever it's call now), from human Splat like The Bound, or Deviant?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends, I wouldn't be surprised at all if certain conspiracies had spreadsheets detailing known monster types and observed phenomenon they can cause. On the flip side low tier hunters may just have no idea that there's different types of monsters at all. Or maybe the reverse, perhaps the conspiracy is keeping its hunters in the dark where as the independent hunters have a long and detailed list they have assembled over their careers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T22:31:15-08:00","id":1529071,"title":"","content":"How do Hunter even decide which are just Human with Supernatural Ability, and Monster? Like a Geist could just be a human with Ghost related Supernatural Merit, or Deviant can just be a person with Psychic Merit, it's even more blur with Minor Template like Skinchanger or Psychic Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T23:01:44-08:00","id":1529074,"title":"","content":"By default, if a person has supernatural powers, hunters don't consider them 'mortal' or mundane. Mages could fall into that category. However, mortals with supernatural merits, as opposed to templates and pseudo-templates, can become hunters.<br /> <br /> The best answer is it depends the hunter and the merit holder in question. The actions of the later matter a lot here. If they are harming people with their powers, that could get them on the Hunter's Target List. If the hunter has encountered a monster with similar abilities (such as a ghost or a Deviant), that could be a be a factor. Different Compacts and Conspiracies can also colour such reactions as well. <br /> <br /> Your average Hunter can't tell the difference between an Urged, Deviant, Mage or 'just' a merit holder from their telekinesis alone. It would basically only come up if they investigate further...kinda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T23:02:29-08:00","id":1529075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1528884-how-do-hunter-compact-and-conspiracy-deal-with-supernatural-mortal?p=1529071#post1529071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Hunter even decide which are just Human with Supernatural Ability, and Monster? Like a Geist could just be a human with Ghost related Supernatural Merit, or Deviant can just be a person with Psychic Merit, it's even more blur with Minor Template like Skinchanger or Psychic Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of times it won't really matter, if someone is going around melting brains it doesn't matter if it's a Deviant or a mortal with a merit, they're a brain melting monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T03:02:07-08:00","id":1529080,"title":"","content":"There is a fiction in Hunter 2e that pretty much leans to this line of thought, where a changeling asks hunters for help to deal with the fetch that stole her place, the fetch is obviously terrified and has no idea what is going on, the changeling however is clearly monstrous and tries to attack the fetch, and the hunters decide in the end to kill the changeling and save the fetch as the fetch is the &quot;person&quot; in question.<br /> <br /> The point is that hunters work on limited information- unless they have some Unseen Sense or special Endowments which allow them to differentiate a &quot;monster&quot; from a &quot;person&quot;, they are going to work with what they have seen and act accordingly.<br /> <br /> Does it mean that a hunter might go around treating a completely regular human being, even without merits, as a &quot;monster&quot; just because the real monster uses them as a &quot;bait and switch&quot;, including suffering from breaking points in reaction to them? Yes, welcome to the witch hunts, try to not get yourself hanged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-21T12:29:55-08:00","id":1529101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1528884-how-do-hunter-compact-and-conspiracy-deal-with-supernatural-mortal?p=1529080#post1529080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a fiction in Hunter 2e that pretty much leans to this line of thought, where a changeling asks hunters for help to deal with the fetch that stole her place, the fetch is obviously terrified and has no idea what is going on, the changeling however is clearly monstrous and tries to attack the fetch, and the hunters decide in the end to kill the changeling and save the fetch as the fetch is the &quot;person&quot; in question.<br /> <br /> The point is that hunters work on limited information- unless they have some Unseen Sense or special Endowments which allow them to differentiate a &quot;monster&quot; from a &quot;person&quot;, they are going to work with what they have seen and act accordingly.<br /> <br /> Does it mean that a hunter might go around treating a completely regular human being, even without merits, as a &quot;monster&quot; just because the real monster uses them as a &quot;bait and switch&quot;, including suffering from breaking points in reaction to them? Yes, welcome to the witch hunts, try to not get yourself hanged.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's honestly my favorite fiction in 2nd edition lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}